              "responseTime": "4431",
              "body": "{\n  \"choices\": [\n    {\n      \"finish_reason\": \"stop\",\n      \"index\": 0,\n      \"message\": {\n        \"content\": \"A large language model primarily learns patterns from text to generate fluent, contextually relevant responses. A reasoning model is designed to perform explicit step-by-step inference, planning, or verification to solve problems more deliberately.\",\n        \"reasoning_content\": \"We need to respond to user: \\\"In two sentences, what is the difference between a large language model and a reasoning model?\\\" Need answer exactly two sentences likely. Need concise. Need maybe mention LLM predicts/generates text based on patterns, reasoning model explicitly performs step-by-step inference/planning/verification to solve problems. Ensure two sentences.\",\n        \"role\": \"assistant\"\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"created\": 1792260047,\n  \"id\": \"chatcmpl-94b2e89d-8cd7-9681-ab62-50b0c3665404\",\n  \"model\": \"qwen3.8-max\",\n  \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\n  \"usage\": {\n    \"completion_tokens\": 114,\n    \"completion_tokens_details\": {\n      \"reasoning_tokens\": 70,\n      \"text_tokens\": 114\n    },\n    \"prompt_tokens\": 79,\n    \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\n      \"cached_tokens\": 0,\n      \"text_tokens\": 79\n    },\n    \"total_tokens\": 193\n  }\n}",
